# Binary artefacts must stay byte-exact. Git for Windows ships with
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which makes Git treat these PDFs as text and
# expand LF to CRLF on checkout. The stored blobs are fine, but the extra bytes
# shift every internal xref offset, so a fresh clone cannot open the file
# ("Unexpected EOF") even though it works in the tree that generated it.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
